{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Midsummer’s Pilgrimage to Nippon’s Fair Shores**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – The Dawn of Arrival in the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\nUpon thy flight’s end thou shalt alight in the grand city of Tokyo where the neon lights do mimic the stars in their brilliance. Dwell first in the quarters of Shinjuku where the towering edifice of the Metropolitan Government Building doth pierce the sky like a spire of old. There take thy rest and marvel at the spectacle of souls in haste below.\n\n**Act I: Scene II – The Gardens of Tranquility**\n\nUpon the morrow thou shalt wander to the Ueno Park where the cherry blossoms if in season shall greet thee with their fleeting beauty. There stroll amongst the temples and museums where history doth whisper from every stone. Let not the bustling streets deter thee for within this verdant oasis peace abounds.\n\n**Act II: Scene I – The Journey to the Ancient Capital**\n\nWith the rising sun of the third day thou shalt embark upon the Shinkansen’s swift steed to Kyoto the ancient seat of emperors and poets. Let the rails carry thee through the land of the setting sun’s hues where rice fields and mountains frame thy passage.\n\n**Act II: Scene II – The Temples of Kyoto’s Glory**\n\nIn Kyoto thou shalt tread the Path of the Philosophers where the gentle flow of the canal doth soothe the spirit. Visit the Golden Pavilion and the Silver one too where the reflections upon the waters do seem a dream of paradise. At the Kiyomizu-dera stand upon the stage and gaze upon the city’s splendor below.\n\n**Act III: Scene I – The Haiku of Nara’s Woods**\n\nA day hence thou shalt venture to Nara where the sacred deer do bow to visitors as if in obeisance to kings. Walk the paths of the Todai-ji where the great Buddha’s visage doth inspire awe and humility. Let the ancient trees of Nara’s forests whisper wisdom to thy soul.\n\n**Act IV: Scene I – The Farewell to Nippon**\n\nAs the sun dips low upon thy final eve thou shalt return to Tokyo to take thy leave of this fair land. In the district of Asakusa walk the Nakamise’s way where trinkets and tales of old are sold. At the Sensoji temple pray for safe travels and a heart ever turned toward the wonders thou hast beheld.\n\n**Epilogue: The Traveler’s Soliloquy**\n\n“O Japan! Thy lands of wonder mine eyes have seen.\nFrom Tokyo’s bright chaos to Kyoto’s serene.\nNara’s whispering woods and the golden spire.\nThy beauty doth live in my heart’s desire.\nFarewell sweet Nippon till again I may tread.\nUpon thy sacred soil where my dreams are fed.”", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.23310025036334991}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.037056177854537964}, {"token": " M", "logprob": -0.7089494466781616}, {"token": "ids", "logprob": -0.0010311054065823555}, {"token": "ummer", "logprob": -5.3165931603871286e-05}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.05013616383075714}, {"token": " Pil", "logprob": -1.2248632907867432}, {"token": "gr", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": "image", "logprob": -1.0132738680113107e-05}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.02282000705599785}, {"token": " Nippon", "logprob": -0.7106702923774719}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.013214274309575558}, {"token": " Fair", "logprob": -0.037988048046827316}, {"token": " Sh", "logprob": -0.8349508047103882}, {"token": "ores", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.531243085861206}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.3601838946342468}, {"token": "Act", "logprob": -0.09308555722236633}, {"token": " I", "logprob": -0.2058342844247818}, {"token": ":", "logprob": -0.12659209966659546}, {"token": " Scene", "logprob": -0.7633951902389526}, {"token": " I", "logprob": -0.4441496729850769}, {"token": " –", "logprob": -0.04735903814435005}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.3221973478794098}, {"token": " Dawn", "logprob": -2.3208882808685303}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.40386053919792175}